        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='42338' id='6' story-point-id='1' type-v2='text' w='40857' x='30054' y='36776'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Welcome to this Story!

Here you can find out about:

- Amount of customers in different states
- Relationship between Income and Customer Lifetime Value
- Distribution of Total Claim Amount within Vehicle Sizes
 
</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='34733' hidden='true' id='7' story-point-id='3' type-v2='text' w='25953' x='57998' y='22247'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Interpretation:

The Regression Plot shows no relationship between Income and Customer Lifetime Value.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Customer Lifetime Value stays quite stable throughout different Incomes.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='46652' hidden='true' id='8' story-point-id='4' type-v2='text' w='37658' x='42969' y='21112'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Interpretation:</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>Although the dispersion of Total Claim Amounts seems to be quite similar for all vehicle sizes, all quartiles are higher up for small vehicles compared to the other two vehicle sizes. This shows that the Total Claim Amounts overall are higher for small vehicles.</run>
            <run fontalignment='0'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontsize='11'>We can see outliers for all vehicle sizes, indicating that the average for all vehicle sizes lays slightly above the median. Outliers with highest Total Claim Amounts are to find in midsize vehicles.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='7264' hidden='true' id='9' story-point-id='6' type-v2='text' w='33313' x='35908' y='44495'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Thank you for exploring the data, I hope you enjoyed the insights!</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
